ype {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439479} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2548bbb-9529-57ff-80c9-7eb2135baee7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440097} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b319f9de-b31e-5b7f-b008-19047e4bc681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439481} {:answer/id #uuid "7743ec0d-8e7c-52c8-b5bf-a2c3ff1639ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7743ec0d-8e7c-52c8-b5bf-a2c3ff1639ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439482} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3fd9d3c-6b34-5cd5-b3aa-e7329f24b386" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440098}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d0d9bc49-c94e-5174-9068-2abf75c42684" :question/math-academy-id "q-128490" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $M$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $det(M)=10$\n- **II.** $det(M)=-5$\n- **III.** $M$ is a singular matrix\n\n \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 4\\end{aligned}|+\\frac{1}{3}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}(12-15)-0+\\frac{1}{3}(0+9\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\cdot (-3)+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =-3\\sqrt{5}+3\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(M)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059849 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f01712c7-1167-5ce2-b75e-faae0fd6dd90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440011} {:answer/id #uuid "b1d67a8b-60f6-5699-b39d-4d178f673f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1d67a8b-60f6-5699-b39d-4d178f673f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440012} :answer-field/id #uuid "61f5a057-7cb0-51ea-b996-75db0a60dff4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440363} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6fca5a5-1769-5de1-b1bf-16320511269e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440013} {:answer/id #uuid "cb641075-be34-57f4-a864-694183e2c508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #