ave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $x=1$\n- **II.** $x=2$\n- **III.** $x=4$" :question/worked-solution "The graph breaks at $x=1,2$ and $4$, meaning that we can't draw the plot without taking our pencil off of the paper when passing through these points.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=1,2,4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083612 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "12a5ad95-0cc9-53c5-8e1c-dae35d1c4447" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Points Where the Normal is Horizontal or Vertical"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0735403-c4cc-5f1c-b3f3-f20e814b4e0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439583} {:answer/id #uuid "18c5b8fc-dc2a-5f66-aba9-2fb2139b0e8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18c5b8fc-dc2a-5f66-aba9-2fb2139b0e8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439584} :answer-field/id #uuid "45f84d85-7a93-543f-94bb-a475c80511cd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440149} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7325a515-140f-5d60-bed7-46dc88237008" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439585} {:answer/id #uuid "76c0b0ff-3576-50aa-ae9a-450fb61d13ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76c0b0ff-3576-50aa-ae9a-450fb61d13ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439586} :answer-field/id #uuid "23d3ed3a-04d8-5745-91e6-80f3e4c230a7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a631b20-d142-5c85-8a98-edc055f0d25f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439587} {:answer/id #uuid "2b5cc863-692b-5dad-a794-3874acf00aa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a631b20-d142-5c85-8a98-edc055f0d25f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439587} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc1b0da1-c6f8-5d48-bed9-a7f7760363df" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440151}] :question/id #uuid "57cb918d-01c6-5793-92dd-c253fd54156c" :question/math-academy-id "q-21080" :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n$x = 4\\cos 2t + 5, y = 5\\sin 2t + 4, 0 \\le t < π$.\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the normal to the curve is horizontal.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $t=0$\n- **II.** $t=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\n- **III.** $t=\\pi$" :question/worked-solution "A vertical tangent (and horizontal normal) requires x′(t)=0 and y′(t)≠0. Here $x′(t)=- 8 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}$ and $y′(t)=10 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}$. Within the given half-open interval the solutions are $\\left\\{0, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right\\}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083613 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083278 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fc81cba-b997-54bc-9e11-0a4ff130833e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Points Where the Tangent is Horizontal or Vertical"}] :question/answer-field